{"name":"Tango","hex":"#d46f31","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tango","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["NATO, ICAO, ITU & IMO radiotelephony clear code (spelling-alphabet name) for the letter T.","Signal flag for the letter T."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tango"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tango","blocks":[{"text":"Tango is a partner and social dance that originated in the 1880s along the Río de la Plata, the natural border between Argentina and Uruguay. The tango was born in the impoverished port areas of these countries from a combination of Argentine Milonga, Spanish-Cuban Habanera, and Uruguayan Candombe celebrations. It was frequently practiced in the brothels and bars of ports, where business owners employed bands to entertain their patrons. It then spread to the rest of the world. A number of variations of this dance currently exist around the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Tango_dancers_in_Montevideo.png/330px-Tango_dancers_in_Montevideo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tango","wikidata":"Q338450"},{"title":"Tango (drink)","blocks":[{"text":"Tango is a British carbonated soft drink brand owned and manufactured by Carlsberg Britvic subsidiary Britvic, primarily marketed in Britain and Ireland. The drink is made and sold in various flavours consisting of real fruit, such as orange, apple, cherry or mango. The Tango brand has also been extended into slushies and non-drink products like bonbon sweets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/21/Tango_drink.JPG/330px-Tango_drink.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tango_(drink)","wikidata":"Q4346256"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Figari-tango32.jpg/500px-Figari-tango32.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Figari-tango32.jpg/500px-Figari-tango32.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"El Tango by Uruguayan painter Pedro Figari","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFigari-tango32.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/TangoPostcard1920.jpg/500px-TangoPostcard1920.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/TangoPostcard1920.jpg/500px-TangoPostcard1920.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tango postcard, c. 1919.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATangoPostcard1920.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Tango-Show-Buenos-Aires-01.jpg/500px-Tango-Show-Buenos-Aires-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Tango-Show-Buenos-Aires-01.jpg/1280px-Tango-Show-Buenos-Aires-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Tango-Show-Buenos-Aires-01.jpg/500px-Tango-Show-Buenos-Aires-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Choreographed stage tango in Buenos Aires, 2005.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATango-Show-Buenos-Aires-01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/MundialTango2011-Escenario.jpg/500px-MundialTango2011-Escenario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/MundialTango2011-Escenario.jpg/500px-MundialTango2011-Escenario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam